.TH ZMQ_PUBLISH.PY 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-downtime-logger 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
zmq_publish.py \- ZeroMQ PUB test producer for the ZmqDetector
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python \-m tools.zmq_publish
.RB [ \-\-endpoint
.IR EP ]
.RB [ \-\-topic
.IR PREFIX ]
.RB [ \-\-state
.BR running | stopped | heartbeat ]
.RB [ \-\-interval
.IR SECS ]
.RB [ \-\-once ]
.RB [ \-\-message
.IR TEXT ]
.br
.B python tools/zmq_publish.py
.I ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Diagnostic tool shipped with
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1).
It
.B binds
a
.B ZMQ_PUB
socket, sleeps 0.3 s so that already\-connecting subscribers finish the
handshake, and then sends one single\-frame UTF\-8 string per interval.
It is the only producer in the Mu2e DAQ tree written for the
.B ZMQ_SUB
socket of
.BR ZmqDetector ;
no production DAQ component publishes run state over
.BR ZMQ_PUB .
Run it from the package root with the virtual environment active.
.PP
The frame is
.I PREFIX
immediately followed by the body (no separator).
The bodies for
.B \-\-state
are
.BR "RUN STATE running" ,
.B RUN STATE stopped
and
.BR "heartbeat tick" .
The detector lowercases the frame and substring\-matches it, so these read
as UP, DOWN and UP (heartbeat) respectively; see
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger\-api (7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-endpoint " EP"
Bind endpoint.
Default
.BR tcp://*:5555 .
5555 is also the port on which
.B mu2edaq\-dashboard
binds its
.B ZMQ_PULL
socket; on a host running the dashboard the bind fails with
.IR "Address already in use" .
Pick another port there and point the detector at it.
.TP
.BI \-\-topic " PREFIX"
Prepended to every body.
Default empty.
Must match the detector's
.B topic
option as a prefix.
.TP
.BR \-\-state " {" running | stopped | heartbeat }
Choose the body.
Default
.BR running .
.TP
.BI \-\-interval " SECS"
Seconds between sends.
Default
.BR 1.0 .
.TP
.B \-\-once
Send one frame and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-message " TEXT"
Send
.I TEXT
as the body instead of the
.B \-\-state
body.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
.B \-\-once
completed.
.TP
.B 1
Bind failure (uncaught
.BR zmq.ZMQError ).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted with Ctrl\-C (the loop runs until interrupted).
.SH EXAMPLES
Publish
.I running
every second on a free port and watch the detector go UP:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python \-m tools.zmq_publish \-\-endpoint tcp://*:5565 \-\-state running
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send a single stop:
.PP
.RS
.nf
python \-m tools.zmq_publish \-\-endpoint tcp://*:5565 \-\-state stopped \-\-once
.fi
.RE
.PP
Matching detector block:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\- id: zmq_run_status
  plugin: downtime_logger.detectors.zeromq_detector:ZmqDetector
  options: {endpoint: "tcp://localhost:5565", heartbeat_timeout_s: 10}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger (1),
.BR mu2edaq\-downtime\-logger\-api (7),
.BR udp_broadcast.py (1)
